          "entry_id": 2978,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.5940733,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "Question: How much will my visit cost if I am paying out-of-pocket?\nAnswer: Out-of-pocket rates are $120 for a General Practitioner (GP) visit, $180 for a Dentist appointment, and $160 for all other specialist consultations.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2991,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.48249534,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n## Medical procedures\n\n- 93000: resting 12-lead electrocardiogram, with the doctor's reading of it - $65\n- 94010: spirometry - $85\n- 93784: 24-hour ambulatory blood pressure monitoring - $140\n- 81002: urine dipstick test done in the clinic - $15\n- 69210: ear wax removal, per ear - $75\n- 17110: wart freezing (cryotherapy), up to 14 warts in one session - $90",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2982,
          "chunk_index": 6,
          "similarity_score": 0.47110558,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Copays and deductibles\n\nYour plan decides how much you pay at the visit. A copay is a fixed amount your plan sets for each visit, and it is collected when you check in. If your plan has a deductible you have not met yet, you pay the amount your plan allows for the visit at check-in. The front desk can estimate that amount for you if you give them your plan details before the visit.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2991,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.43290272,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n\nYour itemized receipt lists each procedure done at your visit by its billing code. Medical procedures use five-digit CPT codes, and dental procedures use CDT codes that start with the letter D. If you pay out of pocket, each procedure below is charged at the price shown, in addition to the rate for the visit at which it is done.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2991,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.4226725,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n## A code you do not recognise\n\nIf your receipt shows a code that is not in this list, the front desk can tell you what it is.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2977,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.4198218,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What should I do if my insurance isn't listed or I am out-of-network?\nAnswer: You can pay out-of-pocket for your visit, and we can provide you with an itemized receipt to submit to your insu",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2991,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.40431082,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n## Dental procedures\n\n- D2391: tooth-coloured filling on one surface of a back tooth - $210\n- D2140: silver (amalgam) filling on one surface - $160\n- D7140: simpl",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2985,
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "similarity_score": 0.39146942,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n## Self-pay vaccine prices\n\nIf your insurance does not cover a vaccine, these are the self-pay prices: flu vaccine $35, high-dose flu vaccine $70, Tdap $55, hepatitis A $85 per dose, ty",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2990,
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "similarity_score": 0.39103156,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# General practice services\n## Medical examinations for work, driving and sport\n\nWe do not carry out commercial driver (DOT) medical examinations, pilot medicals or immigration medical examinations. A",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2979,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.3878504,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: When is payment due, and what payment methods do you accept?\nAnswer: Payment is due at the time of service. We accept cash, major credit and debit cards (Visa, Mastercard, American Express),",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2990,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.37385488,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# General practice services\n## Long-term conditions\n\nIf you live with a long-term condition such as type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, asthma or COPD, your GP will agree a regular review schedule w",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2990,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.35972762,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# General practice services\n## Annual physical examination\n\nAn annual physical is a preventive check-up for adults who feel well. It includes a review of your medical history and current medicines; yo",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2973,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.35377657,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Do I need a referral from a primary care doctor to book with a specialist?\nAnswer: You can book a visit with any of our practitioners without a referral.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2988,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.3423919,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Checking in and registering\n## The self-check-in kiosk\n\nReturning patients can check in at the kiosk beside the front desk instead of queuing. Scan the QR code from your 48-hour reminder text, or ty",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2982,
          "chunk_index": 5,
          "similarity_score": 0.3398696,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Medicare and Medicaid\n\nWe accept Original Medicare (Part B) for medical visits. Medicare does not cover routine dental care, so dental appointments are self-pay for Medicare ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2975,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.3113439,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Do you offer virtual or telehealth consultations?\nAnswer: No, we currently only offer in-person visits at our clinic location.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2990,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.30185893,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# General practice services\n## Minor procedures\n\nWe freeze common warts and verrucas with cryotherapy (liquid nitrogen). A wart may need two to four treatments, about three weeks apart. We do not remo",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2980,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.2947103,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What are your clinic hours and locations?\nAnswer: We are open Monday through Saturday from 9:00 AM to 6:00 PM at 15a Willson St. The nearest free parking is a 3-minute walk away at the Mega ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2988,
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "similarity_score": 0.29381177,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Checking in and registering\n## While you wait\n\nFree guest Wi-Fi is available in the waiting area: the network is called VisitDoc-Guest, and the password is printed on the card at the front desk. Ple",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2988,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.28840113,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Checking in and registering\n## Bringing someone with you\n\nYou may bring one adult companion into the consulting room. Anyone else who comes with you can wait in the waiting area.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2986,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.27869618,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Running late\n## If you are running late\n\nCall the front desk on (212) 555-0142 as soon as you know you will be late, so we can tell the practitioner and plan around it. The phone line is answered Mo",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2984,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.27791378,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Preparing for tests at the clinic\n\nSome tests are done at the clinic during a regular appointment. This guide explains how to prepare for each of them. If your doctor has given you different instruc",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2974,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.27791345,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What should I bring to my first appointment?\nAnswer: Please bring a valid photo ID, your insurance card, and any relevant prior lab or test results related to your case.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2981,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.27399558,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: How early should I arrive before my scheduled appointment time?\nAnswer: If it is your first visit to our clinic, please arrive 15 minutes before your appointment time to complete your regist",
          "text_truncated": true
